273:
(a) Each application for an adult entertainment establishment license shall contain the following information:
(1) The applicant's true full name (including names of officers, members, directors, shareholders and/or partners of business entities) and any other names ever used;
(2) The applicant's present address and telephone number (including officers, members, directors, shareholders and/or partners of business entities);
(3) The applicant's previous addresses and the dates of residence at each address for a period of five years immediately prior to the date of the application (including officers, members, directors, shareholders and/or partners of business entities);
(4) Acceptable written proof that the applicant (including officers, members, directors, shareholders and/or partners of business entities) is at least 21 years of age;
(5) The applicant's (including officers, members, directors, shareholders and/or partners of business entities) height, weight, eye and hair color, and date and place of birth;
(6) Two color photographs of the applicant (including officers, members, directors, shareholders and/or partners of business entities) at least two inches by two inches taken within the last six months, which clearly show the applicant's face;
(7) A statement of the business, occupation and employment history of the applicant (including officers, members, directors, shareholders and/or partners of business entities) for the five years immediately preceding the date of the application;
(8) A statement of the business license history of the applicant (including officers, members, directors, shareholders and/or partners of business entities) and whether said persons or the corporate applicant, in previous operations in this or any other city, state, or territory, has had a license or permit for an adult entertainment business or similar type of business revoked or suspended within the previous five years, the reasons therefor, and the business activities and/or occupations subsequent to such action of suspension or revocation.
(9) If the applicant is a corporation, the name of the corporation shall be set forth exactly as shown in its articles of incorporation or charter, together with the place and date of incorporation, and the names and addresses of each of its current officers and directors and each stockholder holding more than five percent of the stock in the corporation. The same type of information should be set forth for a limited liability company. If the applicant is a partnership, the applicant shall set forth the name, residence address, and dates of birth of the partners, including limited partners. If the applicant is a limited partnership, it shall furnish a copy of its certificate of limited partnership filed with the county clerk. If one or more of the partners is a corporation or limited liability company, the provisions of this subsection 10-41(a)(9) pertaining to corporations and limited liability companies shall apply. The applicant entity shall designate one of its officers, members, or general partners to act as its responsible managing officer. Such designated person shall complete and sign all application forms required of an individual applicant under this section, but only one application fee shall be charged;
(10) The names and addresses of the owner(s) and lessor(s) of the real property upon which the business is to be conducted and a copy of the lease or rental agreement;
(11) If the applicant (including officers, members, directors, shareholders and/or partners of business entities), is not of good moral character as defined in this section, a complete description of any such crime must be provided, including date of violation, date of conviction, jurisdiction, and any disposition, including any fine or sentence imposed and whether terms of disposition have been fully completed;
(12) The applicant's (including officers, members, directors, shareholders and/or partners of business entities) fingerprints;
(13) If the applicant is a person doing business under a trade name, a copy of the properly recorded trade name must be provided. If the applicant is a corporation, the applicant must provide a copy of authority to do business in Georgia, including articles of incorporation; trade name affidavit, if any; and most recent annual report, if any. The same type of information should be set forth for a limited liability company;
(14) A statement that all activities to be carried on in the establishment shall comply with all applicable legal requirements;
(15) Addresses of the premises to be licensed;
(16) Whether the premises are owned or rented and, if the applicant has a right to legal possession of the premises, copies of those documents giving such legal rights;
(17) A plat by a registered engineer, licensed by the State of Georgia, showing the acreage of the proposed site, the location of the proposed adult entertainment establishment in relation to the neighborhood, the surrounding zoning, its proximity to the closest church, school, day care center, library, civic center, public park, playground, governmental building, other adult entertainment establishment; and
(b) Each application for an adult entertainment establishment license shall be verified and acknowledged under oath to be true and correct by:
(1) The applicant, if the applicant is an individual;
(2) The managing or general partner, if a partnership;
(3) The president of the corporation, if a corporation;
(4) The chief administrative official, if any other organization or association.
(Amd. of 2-26-2007, § 1(Exh. A))

